## Failure modes

| What can go wrong | How mtix behaves | What you do |
|---|---|---|
| **Hub unreachable** during push | `mtix sync push` errors with a redacted message; `meta.sync.consecutive_errors` bumps. In MTIX_SYNC_HOOK=1 mode (pre-push hook) it warns and skips. | Retry once connectivity is back. The local queue is durable. |
| **Hub unreachable** during pull | Same — error + bumped counter. Daemon catches up on the next tick. | No action needed if you're not blocked. |
| **Pulled event fails its checks or its apply** (a hub event over the size or clock limits, more than `sync.max_lamport_jump` above your clock, or a dependency whose target has not arrived) | The pull quarantines that event in the local `sync_quarantine` table and applies the rest; the event never changes your clock. Every pull retries the quarantine. `mtix sync status` counts it; `mtix sync doctor` fails its `quarantined events` check. | Run `mtix sync pull` again; if events remain, list them with `mtix sync quarantine list` and take the reasons to whoever runs the hub. Do not delete quarantine rows. `mtix sync clone` refuses while the hub holds such an event: on the fresh store run `mtix sync pull` alone; `mtix sync reconcile --discard-local` deletes local tasks and unpushed changes and needs the ticket count typed at an interactive terminal (no flag supplies it), so it cannot run unattended: only on a store with sync state, after `mtix sync push` and a `pending` 0 in `mtix sync status`; an agent asks the user to run it. |
| **A change is over the 64 KB sync limit** (a long prompt, description, acceptance or comment) | The change is saved locally; with a hub configured a CLI or MCP change warns `WARN: ... over the 65536-byte sync limit` (web UI, REST and gRPC changes do not). `mtix sync push` holds its event (recorded in the local `sync_quarantine` table with source `push`, never sent) and pushes the rest. While a task's creation is held, none of the changes of its subtree are sent: push also holds every event of that task and of the tasks below it, found by the task's internal id so a renumber does not lose one, including changes made after the last push (the admin skill lists the known limits, such as a task whose internal id a merge import changed and that is then renumbered on this machine); and, since a link names its target by number only, every dependency link or unlink made while a creation is held. Once a clock hold on a creation clears, the creation and the changes of its subtree go through the ordinary push, where a renumber by the hub re-addresses the task's changes to the new number before they are sent (MTIX-95.37); a change the hub would refuse stays held under its own reason. A creation held permanently keeps its whole subtree held. An event stamped more than 24h ahead is held only until the clock passes it. `mtix sync status` counts held events; `mtix sync doctor` fails its `held push events` check and names the fix for each. | Follow doctor's fix: shorten or split a field edit and save it again (the new event pushes); raise a held task creation with whoever looks after your sync setup (no automatic re-send); check the clock for a clock hold. Do not delete quarantine rows. |
| **Hub unreachable consecutive ≥ 3** | `mtix_sync_workflow` MCP tool reports `hub-unreachable` and recommends `mtix sync doctor`. | Run `mtix sync doctor`; verify TLS / DSN / connectivity. |
| **Local queue full** (`sync.max_queue_size` cap reached) | Next emit returns `ErrSyncQueueFull` with a remediation message. Event is NOT silently dropped. | Run `mtix sync push --force`, or raise the cap. |
| **Hook bypassed** (`git push --no-verify`) | Local queue retains pending events; hub stays at the older state until next push. | If freshness matters, graduate to the safety-critical workflow's server-side enforcement OR run the daemon. |
| **Schema mismatch** (developer running an older mtix binary) | `mtix sync init` / `clone` refuses with a structured error mentioning the schema version. | Upgrade the local binary (`go install github.com/hyper-swe/mtix/cmd/mtix@latest`). |
| **Mixed mtix versions on the git-tracked `.mtix/tasks.json`** (a teammate still older than 0.5.4) | mtix 0.5.4 writes the file as `schema_version` 2.0.0, with comments and activity. An older client skips it as newer than it supports (`newer than supported — upgrade mtix`), but its next writing command re-exports `.mtix/tasks.json` from its own store, without the comments and changes it skipped. On such a client even an `mtix import` that fails rewrites `.mtix/tasks.json` the same way. A 0.5.4 store is protected from such a file by the auto-import guard: the file carries no comments or activity, so its automatic import is refused and nothing changes. | Upgrade every teammate to 0.5.4 or later. Until then, run no writing commands or `mtix import` on an older client and never commit its `.mtix/tasks.json`. If one was committed, restore `.mtix/tasks.json` from the last good commit in git history, or restore the store from the backup taken before the import (`.mtix/data/backups/pre-sync-<time>.db`; `.mtix/data/pre-sync-backup.db` on 0.5.3 and earlier): stop every mtix process (the MCP server, `mtix serve` and the sync daemon), copy the backup over `.mtix/data/mtix.db`, delete `.mtix/data/mtix.db-wal` and `.mtix/data/mtix.db-shm`, then continue. |
| **Auto-import of `.mtix/tasks.json` refused** after a `git pull` (`mtix: auto-import of .mtix/tasks.json refused`) | The pulled board lacks tasks, comments, comment resolutions, activity entries or dependencies this store holds, or leaves fields empty in a stale copy of a task (one that lacks some of its local activity or has an older `updated_at`). Fields a teammate cleared on purpose apply. Nothing is imported, no backup is taken, the refusal repeats on every command, and writes stay in the store without rewriting the board. An applied import prints one line and keeps the database before it in `.mtix/data/backups/pre-sync-<time>.db` (newest 5 kept). | Read the list, then choose: `mtix import .mtix/tasks.json --mode merge` keeps every local task, comment, activity entry and dependency, and writes nothing while a task's status, assignee, agent state, wake time or deletion state differs from the file's (it lists each conflict; rerun it with `--prefer theirs|ours`, or `--theirs ID,ID` and `--ours ID,ID`, which it records in the task's activity), and decides the other field values per task: when the task's content (title, description, prompt, acceptance, labels) matches the file's, yours win, and otherwise the file's copy wins, undoing your edits to that task; afterwards check `git log -p .mtix/tasks.json` and reapply what it undid (a wrong choice can undo a teammate's claim or your own unclaim), and a task of yours listed as `a different task under this id` (you both created that id) is renumbered to the next number free in both, keeping its uid, and applied only when you rerun with `--confirm`; `mtix sync --fix` keeps the store and rewrites the board; the last resort, `mtix import .mtix/tasks.json --mode replace` (it needs the ticket count typed at an interactive terminal (no flag supplies it)), makes the board win. `mtix sync` shows the refusal until it is resolved. For a conflict although you changed nothing locally (after an upgrade), see [A conflict although nothing changed locally](../TROUBLESHOOTING.md#a-conflict-although-nothing-changed-locally). `sync.auto_sync: false` turns automatic import off for every clone (it is in the tracked `.mtix/config.yaml`), except into an empty store. No write, from the CLI or the MCP server, overwrites a board that changed on disk and was not imported. |
| **Divergent history** (you initialized a hub but a teammate already initialized one with the same project prefix) | `mtix sync init` refuses with `ErrSyncDivergentHistory`. | Either join the existing hub via `mtix sync clone`, or run `mtix sync reconcile --import-as PARENT-ID` to graft your local nodes under a new parent. |
| **Wrong sslmode** in DSN (e.g. `sslmode=disable`) | mtix refuses to connect unless `--insecure-tls` is set AND every host the connection may use is loopback or a local Unix-domain socket. | Fix the DSN to `sslmode=verify-full`. |
| **CA or certificate file unusable** (the CA file named by `sslrootcert`, `MTIX_SYNC_SSLROOTCERT` or `PGSSLROOTCERT`, or the client certificate and key used for TLS, is missing, unreadable or not PEM; when nothing names them, the driver uses `root.crt` from `~/.postgresql/` (`%APPDATA%\postgresql\` on Windows) if it exists, and `postgresql.crt` with `postgresql.key` from the same directory only if both exist) | mtix refuses before connecting to a network host, with a fixed message containing `check the DSN's connection parameters` that repeats neither the path nor the DSN. | Point the setting at a readable PEM file, then run `mtix sync doctor` until it is green. |
| **DSN in a tracked file** | mtix refuses to load DSN from any tracked config; fail-closed at `Source()`. | Move it to `MTIX_SYNC_DSN` env var or `.mtix/secrets` (mode 0600). |
| **Lost laptop with un-pushed events** | The local pending queue dies with the machine; hub never saw those events. | See "Disaster recovery" below — explicit procedure. Recovery is to clone from hub onto a fresh machine. |

